# Context

The user requested a menu control for Claude Code's automatically drafted bug
reports, off by default, and applied every time Claude starts through Ciel
Runtime. The official SendFeedback control is CLAUDE_CODE_SEND_FEEDBACK=0;
this does not disable manual /feedback or send any report.

# Implementation

- Root config claude_feedback_drafts defaults to false. Missing or malformed
  non-boolean stored values remain off; the menu saves true/false explicitly.
- Main menu -> LLM options -> Claude feedback drafts. Enter toggles off/on.
  The same root choice is shown regardless of provider and does not mutate
  provider models, sampling, request caps or timeouts.
- ClaudeEnvironmentProjection.build sets CLAUDE_CODE_SEND_FEEDBACK explicitly
  on native Anthropic, routed and direct-gateway paths. It is a projected key,
  so an inherited value cannot silently retain the preceding launch choice.
- run_claude_session reloads the persisted root choice before every child run,
  including routed/native restarts that do not reselect their model endpoint.
  A launcher regression observes 0 -> 1 -> 0 across three child runs in both
  router and direct mode as the saved choice changes between runs.
- Personal Claude settings, existing feedback drafts and manual /feedback are
  untouched. On does not override account availability, managed policy or the
  user's own Claude feedbackDrafts=off. No automatic sending is added.

# Verification

- evidence/focused-tests.txt: 464 exact-file tests, OK (42 existing retired
  architecture skips). Covers default/old config, invalid values, provider
  independence, native/routed/direct environment, shell projection and repeat
  launches/restarts. The composition root remains at its 4980-line ratchet.
- evidence/menu/verification.okf and result.json: actual production
  portable_prelaunch_menu, Win32 keyboard input, off -> on -> off persisted
  round trip. New owned child processes observed feedback environment 0 ->
  1 -> 0 even when the probe parent carried 1.
- Actual menu console captures: evidence/menu/02-feedback-default-off.txt,
  03-feedback-on.txt and 04-feedback-off.txt. These are actual console-buffer
  text, not generated UI mockups. Pixel capture failed with window not found;
  no PNG is claimed.
- Repository Ruff, compileall, documentation metadata and diff whitespace
  checks passed. Exact commands and results are in evidence/static-checks.txt.

# Boundaries

This is verified working-tree source, not a published or globally installed
release. No commit/push/install or live Claude session restart was performed
for this task. Running Claude children retain their existing environment until
their next launch; each subsequent launch reads the saved choice. No native
feedback draft was triggered or sent in the verification session. Tests and
menu probes used isolated fixture homes/configs/workspaces and owned processes.

